        &lt;dateIssued&gt;2019-11&lt;/dateIssued&gt;\n    &lt;/originInfo&gt;\n    &lt;typeOfResource&gt;text&lt;/typeOfResource&gt;\n    &lt;relatedItem type=&#34;host&#34;&gt;\n        &lt;titleInfo&gt;\n            &lt;title&gt;Proceedings of the 2019 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing and the 9th International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing (EMNLP-IJCNLP)&lt;/title&gt;\n        &lt;/titleInfo&gt;\n        &lt;name type=&#34;personal&#34;&gt;\n            &lt;namePart type=&#34;given&#34;&gt;Kentaro&lt;/namePart&gt;\n            &lt;namePart type=&#34;family&#34;&gt;Inui&lt;/namePart&gt;\n            &lt;role&gt;\n                &lt;roleTerm authority=&#34;marcrelator&#34; type=&#34;text&#34;&gt;editor&lt;/roleTerm&gt;\n            &lt;/role&gt;\n        &lt;/name&gt;\n        &lt;name type=&#34;personal&#34;&gt;\n            &lt;namePart type=&#34;given&#34;&gt;Jing&lt;/namePart&gt;\n            &lt;namePart type=&#34;family&#34;&gt;Jiang&lt;/namePart&gt;\n            &lt;role&gt;\n                &lt;roleTerm authority=&#34;marcrelator&#34; type=&#34;text&#34;&gt;editor&lt;/roleTerm&gt;\n            &lt;/role&gt;\n        &lt;/name&gt;\n        &lt;name type=&#34;personal&#34;&gt;\n            &lt;namePart type=&#34;given&#34;&gt;Vincent&lt;/namePart&gt;\n            &lt;namePart type=&#34;family&#34;&gt;Ng&lt;/namePart&gt;\n            &lt;role&gt;\n                &lt;roleTerm authority=&#34;marcrelator&#34; type=&#34;text&#34;&gt;editor&lt;/roleTerm&gt;\n            &lt;/role&gt;\n        &lt;/name&gt;\n        &lt;name type=&#34;personal&#34;&gt;\n            &lt;namePart type=&#34;given&#34;&gt;Xiaojun&lt;/namePart&gt;\n            &lt;namePart type=&#34;family&#34;&gt;Wan&lt;/namePart&gt;\n            &lt;role&gt;\n                &lt;roleTerm authority=&#34;marcrelator&#34; type=&#34;text&#34;&gt;editor&lt;/roleTerm&gt;\n            &lt;/role&gt;\n        &lt;/name&gt;\n        &lt;originInfo&gt;\n            &lt;publisher&gt;Association for Computational Linguistics&lt;/publisher&gt;\n            &lt;place&gt;\n                &lt;placeTerm type=&#34;text&#34;&gt;Hong Kong, China&lt;/placeTerm&gt;\n            &lt;/place&gt;\n        &lt;/originInfo&gt;\n        &lt;genre authority=&#34;marcgt&#34;&gt;conference publication&lt;/genre&gt;\n    &lt;/relatedItem&gt;\n    &lt;abstract&gt;Modern state-of-the-art Semantic Role Labeling (SRL) methods rely on expressive sentence encoders (e.g., multi-layer LSTMs) but tend to model only local (if any) interactions between individual argument labeling decisions. This contrasts with earlier work and also with the intuition that the labels of individual arguments are strongly interdependent. We model interactions between argument labeling decisions through iterative refinement. Starting with an output produced by a factorized model, we iteratively refine it using a refinement network. Instead of modeling arbitrary interactions among roles and words, we encode prior knowledge about the SRL problem by designing a restricted network architecture capturing non-local interactions. This modeling choice prevents overfitting and results in an effective model, outperforming strong factorized baseline models on all 7 CoNLL-2009 languages, and achieving state-of-the-art results on 5 of them, including English.&lt;/abstract&gt;\n    &lt;identifier type=&#34;citekey&#34;&gt;lyu-etal-2019-semantic&lt;/identifier&gt;\n    &lt;identifier type=&#34;doi&#34;&gt;10.18653/v1/D19-1099&lt;/identifier&gt;\n    &lt;location&gt;\n        &lt;url&gt;https://aclanthology.org/D19-1099/&lt;/url&gt;\n    &lt;/location&gt;\n    &lt;part&gt;\n        &lt;date&gt;2019-11&lt;/date&gt;\n        &lt;extent unit=&#34;page&#34;&gt;\n            &lt;start&gt;1071&lt;/start&gt;\n            &lt;end&gt;1082&lt;/end&gt;\n        &lt;/extent&gt;\n    &lt;/part&gt;\n&lt;/mods&gt;\n&lt;/modsCollection&gt;\n</pre><div class=\"modal-footer pb-1\"><a class=\"btn btn-secondary btn-filesaver disabled\" data-filesaver-target=#citeModsContent data-filesaver-name=D19-1099.xml><i class=\"fas fa-download pe-2\"></i>Download as\nFile</a>\n<button class=\"btn btn-clipboard btn-primary d-none\" data-clipboard-target=#citeModsContent aria-label=\"Copy MODS XML to clipboard\"><i class=\"far fa-clipboard pe-2\"></i>Copy to Clipboard</button></div></div><div class=tab-pane id=citeEndnote role=tabpanel><pre id=citeEndnoteContent class=\"bg-light border p-2\" style=max-height:50vh>%0 Conference Proceedings\n%T Semantic Role Labeling with Iterative Structure Refinement\n%A Lyu, Chunchuan\n%A Cohen, Shay B.\n%A Titov, Ivan\n%Y Inui, Kentaro\n%Y Jiang, Jing\n%Y Ng, Vincent\n%Y Wan, Xiaojun\n%S Proceedings of the 2019 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing and the 9th International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing (EMNLP-IJCNLP)\n%D 2019\n%8 November\n%I Association for Computational Linguistics\n%C Hong Kong, China\n%F lyu-etal-2019-semantic\n%X Modern state-of-the-art Semantic Role Labeling (SRL) methods rely on expressive sentence encoders (e.g., multi-layer LSTMs) but tend to model only local (if any) interactions between individual argument labeling decisions. This contrasts with earlier work and also with the intuition that the labels of individual arguments are strongly interdependent. We model interactions between argument labeling decisions through iterative refinement. Starting with an output produced by a factorized model, we iteratively refine it using a refinement network. Instead of modeling arbitrary interactions among roles and words, we encode prior knowledge about the SRL problem by designing a restricted network architecture capturing non-local interactions. This modeling choice prevents overfitting and results in an effective model, outperforming strong factorized baseline models on all 7 CoNLL-2009 languages, and achieving state-of-the-art results on 5 of them, including English.\n%R 10.18653/v1/D19-1099\n%U https://aclanthology.org/D19-1099/\n%U https://doi.org/10.18653/v1/D19-1099\n%P 1071-1082</pre><div class=\"modal-footer pb-1\"><a class=\"btn btn-secondary btn-filesaver disabled\" data-filesaver-target=#citeEndnoteContent data-filesaver-name=D19-1099.endf><i class=\"fas fa-download pe-2\"></i>Download as\nFile</a>\n<button class=\"btn btn-clipboard btn-primary d-none\" data-clipboard-target=#citeEndnoteContent aria-label=\"Copy Endnote to clipboard\"><i class=\"far fa-clipboard pe-2\"></i>Copy to Clipboard</button></div></div><div class=tab-pane id=citeMarkdown role=tabpanel><h5>Markdown (Informal)</h5><p id=citeMarkdownContent class=\"font-monospace small bg-light border p-2\">[Semantic Role Labeling with Iterative Structure Refinement](https://aclanthology.org/D19-1099/) (Lyu et al., EMNLP-IJCNLP 2019)</p><ul class=mt-2><li><a href=https://aclanthology.org/D19-1099/>Semantic Role Labeling with Iterative Structure Refinement</a> (Lyu et al., EMNLP-IJCNLP 2019)</li></ul><h5>ACL</h5><ul class=mt-2><li id=citeACLstyleContent>Chunchuan Lyu, Shay B. Cohen, and Ivan Titov. 2019. <a href=https://aclanthology.org/D19-1099/>Semantic Role Labeling with Iterative Structure Refinement</a>. In <i>Proceedings of the 2019 Conference on Empirical Methods in Natural Language Processing and the 9th International Joint Conference on Natural Language Processing (EMNLP-IJCNLP)</i>, pages 1071–1082, Hong Kong, China. Association for Computational Linguistics.</li></ul><div class=\"modal-footer pb-1\"><button type=button class=\"btn btn-clipboard btn-primary d-none\" data-clipboard-target=#citeMarkdownContent aria-label=\"Copy Markdown to clipboard\"><i class=\"far fa-clipboard pe-2\"></i>Copy Markdown to\nClipboard</button>\n<button type=button class=\"btn btn-clipboard btn-primary d-none\" data-clipboard-target=#citeACLstyleContent aria-label=\"Copy ACL citation to clipboard\"><i class=\"far fa-clipboard pe-2\"></i>Copy ACL to\nClipboard</button></div></div></div></div></di