/a>\n                            <span class=\"paper-authors\">Shimon Edelman, Nathan Intrator</span>\n                        </div>\n                        \n                    </li>\n                \n            </ul>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n\n<script   src=\"https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.1.min.js\"\n          integrity=\"sha256-/JqT3SQfawRcv/BIHPThkBvs0OEvtFFmqPF/lYI/Cxo=\"   crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/popper.js@1.16.0/dist/umd/popper.min.js\"\n        integrity=\"sha384-Q6E9RHvbIyZFJoft+2mJbHaEWldlvI9IOYy5n3zV9zzTtmI3UksdQRVvoxMfooAo\"\n        crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n<script src=\"https://stackpath.bootstrapcdn.com/bootstrap/4.1.3/js/bootstrap.min.js\"\n        integrity=\"sha384-ChfqqxuZUCnJSK3+MXmPNIyE6ZbWh2IMqE241rYiqJxyMiZ6OW/JmZQ5stwEULTy\"\n        crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n<script>\n    $('.dropdown-menu a.dropdown-toggle').on('click', function (e) {\n        if (!$(this).next().hasClass('show')) {\n            $(this).parents('.dropdown-menu').first().find('.show').removeClass(\"show\");\n        }\n        var $subMenu = $(this).next(\".dropdown-menu\");\n        $subMenu.toggleClass('show');\n\n\n        $(this).parents('li.nav-item.dropdown.show').on('hidden.bs.dropdown', function (e) {\n            $('.dropdown-submenu .show').removeClass(\"show\");\n        });\n\n\n        return false;\n    });\n</script>\n\n\n<script>\ndocument.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {\n    const filters = document.querySelectorAll('.track-filter');\n    const papers = document.querySelectorAll('.paper-list li');\n    const countEl = document.querySelector('.paper-count');\n    const totalCount = papers.length;\n\n    // Build mapping of track slug -> track-N class from filter buttons\n    const trackClassMap = {};\n    filters.forEach(filter => {\n        const track = filter.dataset.track;\n        const trackClass = filter.dataset.trackClass;\n        if (track && trackClass) {\n            trackClassMap[track] = trackClass;\n        }\n    });\n\n    // Apply track classes to paper items\n    papers.forEach(paper => {\n        const track = paper.dataset.track;\n        if (track && trackClassMap[track]) {\n            paper.classList.add(trackClassMap[track]);\n        }\n    });\n\n    // Filter click handlers\n    filters.forEach(filter => {\n        filter.addEventListener('click', function() {\n            const track = this.dataset.track;\n\n            // Update active state\n            filters.forEach(f => f.classList.remove('active'));\n            this.classList.add('active');\n\n            // Filter papers\n            let visibleCount = 0;\n            papers.forEach(paper => {\n                if (track === 'all' || paper.dataset.track === track) {\n                    paper.style.display = '';\n                    visibleCount++;\n                } else {\n                    paper.style.display = 'none';\n                }\n            });\n\n            // Update count\n            if (track === 'all') {\n                countEl.textContent = totalCount + ' papers';\n            } else {\n                countEl.textContent = visibleCount + ' of ' + totalCount + ' papers';\n            }\n        });\n    });\n});\n</script>\n\n\n<br> \n        <div class=\"modal fade\" id=\"myModal\">\n          <div class=\"modal-dialog\">\n            <div class=\"modal-content\">\n              <div class=\"modal-header\">\n                <h4 class=\"modal-title\">Name Change Policy</h4>\n                <button type=\"button pull-right\" class=\"close\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&times;</button>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"modal-body\">\n                <p>Requests for name changes in the electronic proceedings will be accepted with no questions asked.  However name changes may cause bibliographic tracking issues.  Authors are asked to consider this carefully and discuss it with their co-authors prior to requesting a name change in the electronic proceedings.</p>\n\n<p>Use the \"Report an Issue\" link to request a name change.</p>\n\n              </div> \n              <div class=\"modal-footer\">\n\n\n              </div>\n            </div><!-- /.modal-content -->\n          </div><!-- /.modal-dialog -->\n        </div><!-- /.modal -->\n\n\n\n<footer class=\"footer\">\n    <div class=\"btn-spacer\">\n        <a href=\"https://neurips.cc/Help/Contact?select=Conference\">Report an Issue</a> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;|&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;        <a href=\"#\" class=\"modal-link\" data-toggle=\"modal\" data-target=\"#myModal\">Name Change Policy</a>\n    </div>\n\n</footer>\n<div class='hidden'>Do not remove: This comment is monitored to verify that the site is working properly</div>\n<!-- Do not remove: This comment is monitored to verify that the site is working properly -->\n\n</body>\n</html>", "truncated": false, "url": "https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper/2000"}
{"body_sha256": "dfd558b96f2c62cbf2d9ace5b54401366cfcfdad9d36266c54ff915e42dae461", "final_url": "https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper/2016/hash/6709e8d64a5f47269ed5cea9f625f7ab-Abstract.html", "ok": true, "retrieved_at": "2026-10-31T09:45:29.821824+00:00", "text": "\n\n\n\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n\n    <!-- Required meta tags -->\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, shrink-to-fit=no\">\n    <title>Data Programming: Creating Large Training Sets, Quickly</title>\n    <!-- Bootstrap CSS -->\n    <!-- https://codepen.io/surjithctly/pen/PJqKzQ -->\n    <link href=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/bootstrap@5.3.3/dist/css/bootstrap.min.css\" rel=\"stylesheet\" integrity=\"sha384-QWTKZyjpPEjISv5WaRU9OFeRpok6YctnYmDr5pNlyT2bRjXh0JMhjY6hW+ALEwIH\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"https://use.fontawesome.com/releases/v5.8.1/css/all.css\"\n          integrity=\"sha384-50oBUHEmvpQ+1lW4y57PTFmhCaXp0ML5d60M1M7uH2+nqUivzIebhndOJK28anvf\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">\n\n    <!-- Custom CSS (after Bootstrap so it can override) -->\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/static/papers/css/papers.css\">\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/static/papers/css/modern-theme.css?v=15\">\n\n    \n\n    <meta name=\"citation_title\" content=\"Data Programming: Creating Large Training Sets, Quickly\">\n    \n        <meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Ratner, Alexander J.\">\n    \n        <meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"De Sa, Christopher\">\n    \n        <meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Wu, Sen\">\n    \n        <meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Selsam, Daniel\">\n    \n        <meta name=\"citation_author\" content=\"Ré, Christopher\">\n    \n    <meta name=\"citation_journal_title\" content=\"Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems\">\n    <meta name=\"citation_volume\" content=\"29\">\n    \n    \n        \n        \n    \n    \n    <meta name=\"citation_pdf_url\" content=\"https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2016/file/6709e8d64a5f47269ed5cea9f625f7ab-Paper.pdf\">\n    <meta name=\"citation_publication_date\" content=\"2016\">\n\n\n\n\n\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\" async\n            src=\"https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/mathjax/2.7.7/latest.js?config=TeX-MML-AM_CHTML\">\n    </script>\n    <script type=\"text/x-mathjax-config\">\n        MathJax.Hub.Config({\n      \"tex2jax\": {\n        \"inlineMath\": [[\"$\",\"$\"], [\"\\\\(\",\"\\\\)\"]],\n        \"displayMath\": [[\"\\\\[\",\"\\\\]\"]],\n        \"processEscapes\": true\n      }\n    }\n    );\n\n    </script>\n\n    <style>\n        @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {\n            body {\n                background-color: #333;\n                color: #eee;\n            }\n        }\n\n        .btn-spacer {\n            margin: 2px;\n        }\n\n        .footer {\n            position: fixed;\n            left: 0;\n            bottom: 0;\n            width: 100%;\n            background-color: #eee;\n            color: black;\n        }\n\n\n    </style>\n\n</head>\n\n\n<body class=\"modern-theme\">\n\n\n<nav class=\"navbar navbar-expand-md bg-body-tertiary\">\n    <div class=\"container-fluid\">\n        <button class=\"navbar-toggler\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#navbarSupportedContent\" aria-controls=\"navbarSupportedContent\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-label=\"Toggle navigation\">\n            <span class=\"navbar-toggler-icon\"></span>\n        </button>\n        <a class=\"navbar-brand\" href=\"/\">NeurIPS Proceedings</a>\n        <button class=\"navbar-toggler\" type=\"button\" data-bs-toggle=\"collapse\" data-bs-target=\"#navbarSupportedContent\" aria-controls=\"navbarSupportedContent\" aria-expanded=\"false\" aria-label=\"Toggle navigation\">\n            <span class=\"navbar-toggler-icon\"></span>\n        </button>\n        <div class=\"collapse navbar-collapse\" id=\"navbarSupportedContent\">\n            <ul class=\"navbar-nav me-auto mb-2 mb-lg-0\">\n                            <li class=\"nav-item\">\n                <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"/admin/login/?next=/admin/\"><i class=\"fas fa-sign-in-alt\" title=\"Login\"></i></a>\n            </li>\n            <li class=\"nav-item\">\n                <a class=\"nav-link\" href=\"/admin/logout/?nextp=/admin\"><i class=\"fas fa-sign-out-alt\" title=\"Logout\"></i></a>\n            </li>\n\n            </ul>\n            <form class=\"d-flex\" role=\"search\" method=\"get\" role=\"search\" action=\"/papers/search\">\n                <input class=\"form-control me-2\" type=\"search\" placeholder=\"Search\" aria-label=\"Search\" name=\"q\">\n                <button class=\"btn btn-outline-success\" type=\"submit\">Search</button>\n            </form>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n</nav>\n\n\n\n\n<div class=\"container-fluid\">\n    <div class=\"col p-3 paper-detail\">\n\n    \n        <header class=\"paper-header\">\n            <h1 class=\"paper-title\">Data Programming: Creating Large Training Sets, Quickly</h1>\n            <p class=\"paper-authors\">Alexander J Ratner, Christopher M De Sa, Sen Wu, Daniel Selsam, Christopher Ré</p>\n            <p class=\"paper-meta\">\n                <a href=\"/paper_files/paper/2016\">Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems 29  (NIPS 2016)</a>\n                \n                \n            </p>\n        </header>\n\n        <div class=\"paper-actions\"><a class='btn btn-light btn-spacer' href='/paper_files/paper/2016/file/6709e8d64a5f47269ed5cea9f625f7ab-Bibtex.bib'>Bibtex</a> <a class='btn btn-light btn-spacer' href='/paper_files/paper/2016/file/6709e8d64a5f47269ed5cea9f625f7ab-Metadata.json'>Metadata</a> <a class='btn btn-light btn-spacer' href='/paper_files/paper/2016/file/6709e8d64a5f47269ed5cea9f625f7ab-Paper.pdf'>Paper</a> <a class='btn btn-light btn-spacer' href='/paper_files/paper/2016/file/6709e8d64a5f47269ed5cea9f625f7ab-Reviews.html'>Reviews</a> <a class='btn btn-light btn-spacer' href='/paper_files/paper/2016/file/6709e8d64a5f47269ed5cea9f625f7ab-Supplemental.zip'>Supplemental</a></div>\n\n        \n\n        <section class=\"paper-section\">\n            <h2 class=\"section-label\">Abstract</h2>\n            <p class=\"paper-abstract\"><p>Large labeled training sets are the critical building blocks of supervised learning methods and are key enablers of deep learning techniques. For some applications, creating labeled training sets is the most time-consuming and expensive part of applying machine learning. We therefore propose a paradigm for the programmatic creation of training sets called data programming in which users provide a set of labeling functions, which are programs that heuristically label subsets of the data, but that are noisy and may conflict. By viewing these labeling functions as implicitly describing a generative model for this noise, we show that we can recover the parameters of this model to \"denoise\" the generated training set, and establish theoretically that we can recover the parameters of these generative models in a handful of settings. We then show how to modify a discriminative loss function to make it noise-aware, and demonstrate our method over a range of discriminative models including logistic regression and LSTMs. Experimentally, on the 2014 TAC-KBP Slot Filling challenge, we show that data programming would have led to a new winning score, and also show that applying data programming to an LSTM model leads to a TAC-KBP score almost 6 F1 points over a state-of-the-art LSTM baseline (and into second place in the competition). Additionally, in initial user studies we observed that data programming may be an easier way for non-experts to create machine learning models when training data is limited or unavailable.</p>\n</p>\n        </section>\n\n    \n\n    </div>\n</div>\n\n\n<script   src=\"https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.1.min.js\"\n          integrity=\"sha256-/JqT3SQfawRcv/BIHPThkBvs0OEvtFFmqPF/lYI/Cxo=\"   crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n<script src=\"https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/popper.js@1.16.0/dist/umd/popper.min.js\"\n        integrity=\"sha384-Q6E9RHvbIyZFJoft+2mJbHaEWldlvI9IOYy5n3zV9zzTtmI3UksdQRVvoxMfooAo\"\n        crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n<script src=\"https://stackpath.bootstrapcdn.com/bootstrap/4.1.3/js/bootstrap.min.js\"\n        integrity=\"sha384-ChfqqxuZUCnJSK3+MXmPNIyE6ZbWh2IMqE241rYiqJxyMiZ6OW/JmZQ5stwEULTy\"\n        crossorigin=\"anonymous\"></script>\n<script>\n    $('.dropdown-menu a.dropdown-toggle').on('click', function (e) {\n        if (!$(this).next().hasClass('show')) {\n            $(this).parents('.dropdown-menu').first().find('.show').removeClass(\"show\");\n        }\n        var $subMenu = $(this).next(\".dropdown-menu\");\n        $subMenu.toggleClass('show');\n\n\n        $(this).parents('li.nav-item.dropdown.show').on('hidden.bs.dropdown', function (e) {\n            $('.dropdown-submenu .show').removeClass(\"show\");\n        });\n\n\n        return false;\n    });\n</script>\n\n\n\n\n<br> \n        <div class=\"modal fade\" id=\"myModal\">\n          <div class=\"modal-dialog\">\n            <div class=\"modal-content\">\n              <div class=\"modal-header\">\n                <h4 class=\"modal-title\">Name Change Policy</h4>\n                <button type=\"button pull-right\" class=\"close\" data-dismiss=\"modal\" aria-hidden=\"true\">&times;</button>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"modal-body\">\n                <p>Requests for name changes in the electronic proceedings will be accepted with no questions asked.  However name changes may cause bibliographic tracking issues.  Authors are asked to consider this carefully and discuss it with their co-authors prior to requesting a name change in the electronic proceedings.</p>\n\n<p>Use the \"Report an Issue\" link to request a name change.</p>\n\n              </div>